  "body": "I have been experimenting with 2.4GHz LoRa modules using LoRa modulation (MeshCore using RadioLib 7.7.1).\n\nDuring my tests I discovered SX1281 & SX1280 devices could communicate with each other but not with an LR1121, when using SF 11 or 12 and 406.25 KHz bandwidth.\nIf the LR1121 is set forceLDRO on for SF11 & 12, the module communicates with the SX128x modules as expected at all bandwidths.\nFor the SX128x compatible bandwidths (203.125, 406.25, 806.5) the current LR1121 symbol time based calculation gives only combination 203.125 / SF12 as requiring LRDO. In testing this is the only compatible SF11+ combination between the two modules currently (without use of forceLDRO).\n\n\nThe SX128x datasheet makes no mention of low data rate optimization. The LR1121 datasheet does not indicate this as being a requirement for compatibility. \nHowever, reading the LR2021 datasheet (section 9.9.1 SetLoraModulationParams, under table 9-4) I found this gem:\n\nRecommended settings for ldro are:\n* 0 for SF5-10, BW250 / SF11, BW500, BW1000\n* 1 for all other BW and SF11/12 (including SX1280 compatible bandwidths BW800/400/200)\n\nIt would seem Semtech thinks this is a requirement for SX128x compatibility, at SF11/12, with the LR2021.\nUnfortunately I don't have a LR2021 to test this with currently. \n\nThe auto LDRO calculation seems common to both devices, possibly a change to accommodate SX128x compatibility would be beneficial.",
